WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.420
- [Instructor] We are told
that Tony has 2/3 of a bag

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.910
of dark chocolate chips

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.720
and 4/5 of a bag of white chocolate chips.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.230
Determine a reasonable estimate

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.810
of the total amount of
chocolate chips Tony has.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:16.790
So pause this video

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.170
and see if you can figure
out which of these choices

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.040
is the best reasonable estimate

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.333
of the total amount of chocolate chips.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.010
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.230
Now in the future,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.110
we will learn how to actually
add something like 2/3

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.180
to 4/5, but for the sake of this exercise,

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.450
we just want to get good at estimating it.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.820
And one way to estimate
is to try to visualize.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.570
So let's make,

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.490
so this is a whole right over here,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:52.420
and then this is another
whole right over there.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.870
Try to make them the same size.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.900
Now what does 2/3 look like?

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.570
Well, let me divide this
into three equal sections,

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.990
so that is pretty close.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.290
It's hand drawn, so it's not perfect,

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:04.730
but I think it gets the job done.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:08.020
And 2/3 would be, that's
1/3 right over there

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.870
and then that is 2/3 right there,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.470
and what does 4/5 looks like?

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.303
Well, let's see.

00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:16.320
I can divide this into fifths,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.140
so 1/5, 2/5,

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.500
3/5, and then 4/5, and 5/5.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.470
That is pretty good.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.620
And now what does 4/5 look like?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.230
Well, it would be 1/5,

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:34.540
2/5, 3/5, and then 4/5.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.130
So if we were to add these two together,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.670
do we have less than 1/2 of a bag,

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.570
more than 1/2 of a bag,
but less than one bag,

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.870
or more than one bag?

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.660
Well, when you see even the first 2/3,

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.290
where is a half?

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.800
A half would have been right around there

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.150
if we're talking about half of it.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:57.730
So 2/3 is more than a half,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:01.150
and then we also see that
4/5 is more than a half.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.660
If you had a half,

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.470
it would have been like this far.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.280
So you can see that you're
adding two things together

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.140
that are both more than a half.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.350
And if you have two halves of
something, that'd be a whole,

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.140
so if you have two things
that are more than a half,

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.080
if you add them together,

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.120
you're gonna have more than
a bag of chocolate chips.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.070
So I like this choice right over here.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.320
Let's do another example.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.220
So here, we are told

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.700
that a banana weights 3/8 of a kilogram,

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.300
an apple weighs 2/3 of a kilogram.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.960
Determine a reasonable estimate

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.750
for the weight of both fruits.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.820
So pause this video again

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.170
and see if you can have a go at that.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.730
All right, so the key is that we need

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.420
to determine a reasonable estimate.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.070
So let's actually just try
to represent these again,

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.450
so how could I represent 3/8 of something,

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.310
of a kilogram, in this case?

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:53.660
Well, let me draw a rectangle here

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.320
and I'm going to try to
divide it into eighths,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.450
eight equal sections,

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.680
so that looks about a half.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.490
Let me do it right over there.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.630
That looks like about a half,

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.910
and then if I were to divide those,

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.450
these would be fourths,

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.950
and this is hand drawn,
so it's not perfect,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.110
but it will help us
understand things a bit.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:16.790
So then let me divide these,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.150
and so this would get me to eighths.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.610
So I have eight sections here.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.720
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.960
and if I'm talking about three

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.260
of those eight equal sections,

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.260
I'd have 1/8, 2/8, and 3/8,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.170
so that is 3/8 right over there

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.520
and what does 2/3 looks like?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.120
So I'll do that in purple,

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.260
so if this is a whole,

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.580
this is a whole like that.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.600
If I divide it into three equal sections,

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:48.140
it's going to be something like that.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.640
I could draw it a little bit better,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.950
so something like that,

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.790
and so two of those three equal sections,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:58.200
that's 1/3, and so that is 2/3.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.050
Now what happens if I try to
add these things together?

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.160
Well one thing I could try
to do to help visualize

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.810
is I could take that piece there.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.860
The wholes are roughly the same length

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.534
or I tried to draw them

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:10.640
so that they are roughly the same length,

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.600
and if I were to copy and paste that

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.360
and move that over here,

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.790
it looks like, if I were to estimate it,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.580
I'm getting pretty close
to a whole kilogram here.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:24.930
So it's definitely not just
about 1/3 of a kilogram.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.590
1/3 of a kilogram would be just one

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.800
of these three equal sections.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.420
We're way more than that,
so we rule that out.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.430
About one kilogram, that's what we saw.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.310
When we,

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:39.950
when we take the 2/3 and add to that, 3/8,

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:43.010
where it looks like, and
once again, we're estimating.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.190
We don't know exactly.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.270
It looks like we're a
little bit over a kilogram,

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.520
so I like this choice,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.510
and we're no where close to two kilograms.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.990
Two kilograms, we would be
filling in another whole

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.960
on top of this one right over here.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.853
So it's not that choice either.

